Subject: [PATCH] Add inref operator

Predicate to list changes included in a ref.

Change-Id: I59b4c166e77c93d46d050eb24e97e18320586317
---
 Documentation/user-search.txt                      |   21 ++++++++
 .../google/gerrit/client/SearchSuggestOracle.java  |    2 +
 .../server/query/change/ChangeQueryBuilder.java    |    6 ++
 .../gerrit/server/query/change/InRefPredicate.java |   54 ++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 83 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 gerrit-server/src/main/java/com/google/gerrit/server/query/change/InRefPredicate.java

diff --git a/Documentation/user-search.txt b/Documentation/user-search.txt
index f4328be..f031f2b 100644
--- a/Documentation/user-search.txt
+++ b/Documentation/user-search.txt
@@ -168,6 +168,27 @@ message:'MESSAGE'::
 +
 Changes that match 'MESSAGE' arbitrary string in the commit message body.
 
+[[inref]]
+inref:'REF'::
++
+Changes which are included in any fully qualified ref and if unqualified,
+matches a 'BRANCH' or 'TAG'. This operator by default matches on open
+changes only. Pair with 'status:merged' to match on merged changes.
+
+`inref:foo status:merged`::
++
+Matches all changes included in the ref: foo. If more than one
+ref with the same name is found(ex: refs/heads/foo and refs/tags/foo),
+then changes included in either of them are matched.
+
+`inref:refs/heads/bar status:merged`::
++
+Matches all changes included in branch: bar
+
+`inref:refs/tags/baz status:merged`::
++
+Matches all changes included in tag: baz
+
 [[file]]
 file:^'REGEX'::
 +
